1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:03,100
In his third year of working life.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:08,367
Okay, let's get ready so we can roughly explain what we
just discussed to the client by the next mee

3
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:09,233
Yes.

4
00:00:09,967 --> 00:00:12,400
- If there's anything you don't get, ask me.
- Okay~

5
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:14,367
It's "yes."

6
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:15,333
Yes!

7
00:00:18,367 --> 00:00:20,067
Well, I'm heading out for the day.

8
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:21,333
The gym?

9
00:00:22,167 --> 00:00:24,867
Not the gym today. I've got dinner plans.

10
00:00:24,867 --> 00:00:29,500
Oh? Dinner out? That's rare for you.
Is it someone from work?

11
00:00:32,033 --> 00:00:37,233
- A high school classmate.
- Huh, Yamamura-san has friends?

12
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:38,300
Hey.

13
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:40,833
I'm not insulting you.

14
00:00:41,633 --> 00:00:43,667
It sounded like an insult.

15
00:00:44,767 --> 00:00:49,633
I just meant you seem like someone who
keeps people at a distance.

16
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:53,600
Is that so.

17
00:00:56,367 --> 00:00:58,367
- Do you have a photo?
- Huh?

18
00:01:04,867 --> 00:01:05,967
Oh, you're actually going to show me.

19
00:01:09,633 --> 00:01:11,100
He's a man.

20
00:01:12,467 --> 00:01:13,367
Yeah. So?

21
00:01:14,267 --> 00:01:15,267
Is he your boyfriend?

22
00:01:15,767 --> 00:01:16,267
What?

23
00:01:16,567 --> 00:01:17,967
Why would you think that?

24
00:01:17,967 --> 00:01:20,033
It's not that unusual, you know.

25
00:01:21,033 --> 00:01:26,167
Besides, this guy looks really happy.

26
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:40,600
...You're right. He does.

27
00:01:44,967 --> 00:01:45,833
Okay, I'm off.

28
00:01:46,733 --> 00:01:48,367
Good work today.

29
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:55,833
He didn't deny it.

30
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:16,133
Hayama-san, do you have a minute?

31
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:17,600
What is it, Iida-san?

32
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:20,667
It's about the new screen.
Could you take a look?

33
00:02:22,367 --> 00:02:24,400
I'm glad we went with this spec after all.

34
00:02:24,833 --> 00:02:26,700
That's thanks to your advice, Iida-san.

35
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:28,167
Oh, no. It's just my job.

36
00:02:28,767 --> 00:02:29,833
You're always a big help.

37
00:02:42,367 --> 00:02:44,000
You seem to be in a good mood.

38
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:45,600
Huh? Can you tell?

39
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,233
Of course, with a face that happy.

40
00:02:49,133 --> 00:02:51,933
Today's my monthly dinner with a
high school classmate.

41
00:02:52,567 --> 00:02:54,833
Every month? You two must be close.

42
00:02:56,067 --> 00:02:56,933
Do you think so?

43
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,767
- Oh, that's why you finished today's tasks early.
- Yes, I did.

44
00:03:02,767 --> 00:03:05,300
If you kept this pace up, it'd
help me too.

45
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:05,933
I can't do this every day.

46
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,067
Midori...

47
00:03:23,067 --> 00:03:24,200
Yes!

48
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:26,333
Sorry.

49
00:03:34,633 --> 00:03:37,067
He's so easy to read.

50
00:03:37,067 --> 00:03:38,967
Like a baby.

51
00:03:40,200 --> 00:04:21,267
♪

52
00:04:27,667 --> 00:04:30,333
Sorry to keep you waiting! Hayama here.

53
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:32,933
So, how have you been lately?

54
00:04:34,100 --> 00:04:35,633
Same as usual, I guess.

55
00:04:35,633 --> 00:04:39,733
Oh, a consultant recently joined us,
and we talk quite a bit.

56
00:04:39,733 --> 00:04:41,433
Oh yeah? What's he like?

57
00:04:42,300 --> 00:04:46,667
Um... kind of hard to read.

58
00:04:47,900 --> 00:04:51,000
- He's the exact opposite of you.
- Yeah, he is.

59
00:04:51,433 --> 00:04:54,567
Oh, what about you, Midori? That
intense junior of yours?

60
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:57,600
Ah, same as ever. Even with his senior,

61
00:04:57,600 --> 00:04:59,833
he asks all sorts of blunt
questions. Intense guy.

62
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:04,333
But I do know he's not a bad guy.

63
00:05:05,533 --> 00:05:07,867
Lucky... I envy that junior spot, Midori.

64
00:05:08,367 --> 00:05:09,900
I'm so jealous.

65
00:05:10,667 --> 00:05:13,000
What's that supposed to mean?

66
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,967
A mere junior wouldn't get
dinner like this.

67
00:05:16,333 --> 00:05:17,767
That would be sad.

68
00:05:18,867 --> 00:05:19,567
Isn't it?

69
00:05:28,133 --> 00:05:30,067
Why do you meet with me?

70
00:05:31,233 --> 00:05:32,200
I don't know.

71
00:05:40,067 --> 00:05:42,433
Think about it before we meet next time.

72
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:51,600
That answer...

73
00:05:52,900 --> 00:05:54,767
I never did get to hear it.

74
00:05:57,767 --> 00:05:58,333
What's wrong?

75
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:00,033
Oh, nothing.

76
00:06:01,867 --> 00:06:06,733
I never imagined in high school that I'd be
drinking with you like this, Midori.

77
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:09,133
Yeah.

78
00:06:09,867 --> 00:06:11,133
The only people I meet up with like this

79
00:06:11,133 --> 00:06:12,567
are you and Yoshida.

80
00:06:13,167 --> 00:06:14,800
Huh? Same as Yoshida?

81
00:06:15,633 --> 00:06:17,900
- Why are you competing?
- But...

82
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:21,600
You meet up with Arisa
regularly too, don't you?

83
00:06:22,133 --> 00:06:23,533
It's the same thing.

84
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:25,467
Well, that's true, but...

85
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:28,000
Well...

86
00:06:29,667 --> 00:06:31,533
I do see you more often.

87
00:06:37,633 --> 00:06:38,800
By a little.

88
00:06:48,667 --> 00:06:50,267
Midori.

89
00:06:51,833 --> 00:06:53,100
Let's go to dinner next month, too.

90
00:06:55,267 --> 00:06:56,500
I'm looking forward to it.

91
00:06:57,167 --> 00:06:57,767
To our dinners.

92
00:07:00,533 --> 00:07:01,900
Mm.

93
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:07,233
If I give an answer,

94
00:07:12,167 --> 00:07:14,967
I feel like this relationship
will disappear.

95
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,000
Well, then.

96
00:07:22,767 --> 00:07:25,200
See you.

97
00:07:50,367 --> 00:07:51,233
What do I...

98
00:07:54,333 --> 00:07:56,267
want to do, I wonder?

99
00:08:13,567 --> 00:08:15,400
Okay, how's this?

100
00:08:16,867 --> 00:08:17,767
Looks good.

101
00:08:18,333 --> 00:08:19,000
Thanks.

102
00:08:19,667 --> 00:08:23,167
- I hope your mom likes it.
- She will.

103
00:08:23,767 --> 00:08:24,700
She loves flowers.

104
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:28,667
Oh, Midori, welcome.

105
00:08:28,667 --> 00:08:29,767
It's been a while.

106
00:08:30,233 --> 00:08:31,433
What brings you in today?

107
00:08:31,433 --> 00:08:34,200
It's Midori's mother's
birthday, apparently.

108
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:37,167
Oh, how wonderful.

109
00:08:37,667 --> 00:08:39,000
Thank you.

110
00:08:39,799 --> 00:08:42,667
You came to buy a present
before, too, didn't you?

111
00:08:43,200 --> 00:08:45,800
Was it for your teacher?

112
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:47,900
That was at my coming-of-age ceremony.

113
00:08:50,333 --> 00:08:52,267
Come to think of it, at your
coming-of-age ceremony,

114
00:08:52,267 --> 00:08:54,000
you were really wild, Midori.

115
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,667
Exactly.

116
00:08:56,567 --> 00:08:59,167
Sorry if I caused any trouble.

117
00:08:59,167 --> 00:09:04,333
It's fine. Drinking can bring out
feelings you didn't expect to reveal.

118
00:09:04,833 --> 00:09:07,000
It's not necessarily a bad thing.

119
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:08,533
True feelings...

120
00:09:10,633 --> 00:09:11,633
Do you remember?

121
00:09:11,867 --> 00:09:12,767
Midori?

122
00:09:17,133 --> 00:09:18,300
Vaguely.

123
00:09:19,267 --> 00:09:20,333
Faintly.

124
00:09:37,700 --> 00:09:38,967
Cheers!

125
00:09:39,467 --> 00:09:40,367
Hey, cheers!

126
00:09:40,367 --> 00:09:41,000
Here's to us!

127
00:09:41,233 --> 00:09:42,400
Booze! Bottoms up!

128
00:09:42,567 --> 00:09:46,433
Yeah! Me too! Adulthood rocks!

129
00:09:46,433 --> 00:09:48,733
- I can really hold my liquor!
- Me too! Me too!

130
00:09:48,733 --> 00:09:53,167
If you get too drunk, I'll dump water
on your head in the street.

131
00:09:53,167 --> 00:09:57,000
Don't say scary things. Coming from
you, it sounds serious.

132
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,167
Ha ha. I am serious.

133
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,033
What about you, Midori?

134
00:10:02,033 --> 00:10:03,000
Are you drunk?

135
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:05,333
Not really.

136
00:10:06,533 --> 00:10:10,267
Midori's been an adult for a while now,
hasn't he? You were born in May.

137
00:10:11,267 --> 00:10:14,500
Yeah, it's been over half a year.

138
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:17,767
Hayama is still a minor, isn't he?

139
00:10:17,767 --> 00:10:20,033
I think he said his birthday's in March.

140
00:10:22,067 --> 00:10:24,367
Why does Hayama come into this?

141
00:10:24,367 --> 00:10:26,633
Huh? Don't you still meet up
with him sometimes?

142
00:10:33,100 --> 00:10:34,433
Not lately.

143
00:10:37,067 --> 00:10:38,633
Ah, so that's how it is.

144
00:10:38,633 --> 00:10:40,600
What do you mean, "so that's how it is"?

145
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:43,933
Oh, nothing. I just kind of thought so.

146
00:10:44,467 --> 00:10:47,433
What's with that look, like
you know everything?

147
00:10:47,433 --> 00:10:49,433
Huh? Do I look like that?

148
00:10:49,733 --> 00:10:54,033
Yeah, you do. That's exactly the
face you're making.

149
00:10:54,033 --> 00:10:56,967
Oh, are you maybe pretty drunk, Midori?

150
00:10:57,900 --> 00:10:59,700
I'm not drunk.

151
00:11:00,467 --> 00:11:05,167
So Yamamura's a bad drunk.
He's an angry drunk.

152
00:11:05,167 --> 00:11:07,300
Ugh, shut up already.

153
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:10,467
- Let me kiss you!
- Hey, stop it!

154
00:11:10,467 --> 00:11:12,600
- Cut it out!
- A kiss? Seriously?

155
00:11:12,800 --> 00:11:15,833
- Whoa, whoa, whoa!
- Kiss!

156
00:11:15,833 --> 00:11:17,333
Okay, okay. Midori, calm down.

157
00:11:17,333 --> 00:11:20,433
Yoshida, let me kiss you!

158
00:11:20,433 --> 00:11:21,933
No, none of that.

159
00:11:22,467 --> 00:11:23,133
Why not?

160
00:11:23,467 --> 00:11:26,367
- You'll definitely regret it later, Midori.
- What?

161
00:11:26,833 --> 00:11:28,633
Then, Yamamura, kiss me instead!

162
00:11:30,767 --> 00:11:37,267
Come on, kiss me!

163
00:11:43,667 --> 00:11:46,367
Come on, Midori.

164
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,933
Why are you getting in the way?

165
00:11:51,167 --> 00:11:52,433
Getting in the way?

166
00:12:01,033 --> 00:12:02,667
Do you want to that badly?

167
00:12:05,467 --> 00:12:06,500
I do.

168
00:12:12,333 --> 00:12:13,300
With who?

169
00:12:39,700 --> 00:12:41,800
I can't say.

170
00:12:53,533 --> 00:12:56,100
I hope you can say it someday.

171
00:13:03,367 --> 00:13:04,467
Yamamura-san.

172
00:13:05,033 --> 00:13:05,900
Are you okay?

173
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:08,000
Is something wrong?

174
00:13:11,033 --> 00:13:12,800
Ah, kind of.

175
00:13:19,367 --> 00:13:21,167
Did you just remember something
embarrassing from your past?

176
00:13:23,333 --> 00:13:25,300
Why are you so weirdly sharp?

177
00:13:26,467 --> 00:13:27,700
Is it about romance?

178
00:13:30,267 --> 00:13:30,933
Romance...

179
00:13:34,633 --> 00:13:36,433
It's fine to agonize over it,

180
00:13:36,933 --> 00:13:40,900
but please only get down to the extent
that it doesn't affect your work.

181
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:43,900
Hey, is that something to say
to your senior?

182
00:13:44,800 --> 00:13:46,467
It's better to say what you want to say.

183
00:13:54,433 --> 00:13:56,700
What's with that guy?

184
00:13:59,933 --> 00:14:01,433
There's no way I could say it.

185
00:14:03,967 --> 00:14:06,400
That I find his honesty cute,

186
00:14:08,833 --> 00:14:11,433
or that I'm happy when he
comes up to me smiling.

187
00:14:12,433 --> 00:14:13,233
Isn't that strange?

188
00:14:15,933 --> 00:14:17,633
It's not strange at all.

189
00:14:18,933 --> 00:14:21,233
That you can say that so
straightforwardly...

190
00:14:28,300 --> 00:14:29,067
Romance, huh...

191
00:14:40,700 --> 00:14:42,500
Hayama-san, are you finishing up?

192
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:44,733
Yes, I'm off.

193
00:14:47,400 --> 00:14:48,833
Is it that dinner again?

194
00:14:49,667 --> 00:14:51,100
Huh? How do you know?

195
00:14:51,300 --> 00:14:56,167
- It's obvious from your face.
- Oh... is it?

196
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:03,767
You like him, don't you?

197
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,233
Eh?

198
00:15:06,267 --> 00:15:07,033
That person.

199
00:15:08,333 --> 00:15:09,867
How can you tell?

200
00:15:09,867 --> 00:15:12,133
Like I said, it shows on your face.

201
00:15:13,067 --> 00:15:13,767
I see.

202
00:15:17,933 --> 00:15:20,667
He probably realizes, you know.

203
00:15:22,100 --> 00:15:24,167
- I don't think so.
- Really?

204
00:15:24,167 --> 00:15:25,000
Yes.

205
00:15:26,867 --> 00:15:28,267
If he'd noticed, I don't think

206
00:15:28,933 --> 00:15:30,933
he'd meet me this often.

207
00:15:35,733 --> 00:15:38,033
Oh, then I'll head out first.

208
00:15:38,633 --> 00:15:40,000
Take care.

209
00:15:47,567 --> 00:15:50,267
Maybe he's meeting me because he knows.

210
00:15:52,767 --> 00:15:55,400
I work from home a lot, so I'm not
getting enough exercise.

211
00:15:56,033 --> 00:15:57,167
Go to the gym.

212
00:15:57,733 --> 00:16:00,067
Midori, do you think I'd go?

213
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:02,900
No, I don't.

214
00:16:03,367 --> 00:16:04,233
Right?

215
00:16:04,967 --> 00:16:07,800
- Just moving around isn't fun.
- Is it?

216
00:16:08,633 --> 00:16:11,167
Pushing yourself is the fun part.

217
00:16:11,167 --> 00:16:14,267
That's just your thing, Midori.

218
00:16:15,067 --> 00:16:20,667
- Muscles don't lie.
- Hmm...

219
00:16:20,667 --> 00:16:23,233
- Don't you agree?
- See? There you go again.

220
00:16:23,833 --> 00:16:24,800
Ha ha ha...

221
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:27,233
Ah, this is fun.

222
00:16:27,233 --> 00:16:29,567
I'm glad I worked hard to
finish my work today.

223
00:16:29,567 --> 00:16:31,833
- Me too.
- Huh?

224
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:32,800
You too, Midori?

225
00:16:33,167 --> 00:16:36,167
Well, I don't want overtime
eating into dinner.

226
00:16:36,767 --> 00:16:37,533
Oh, okay.

227
00:16:38,467 --> 00:16:42,667
That makes me happy. I look
forward to it every month.

228
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:59,000
Is everything alright?

229
00:17:00,267 --> 00:17:02,767
It's just that person offering to set
me up with a woman again.

230
00:17:06,233 --> 00:17:09,133
He never gives up. I keep telling
him I'm done with that.

231
00:17:10,067 --> 00:17:10,567
Wait, what?

232
00:17:11,933 --> 00:17:13,000
You're done with that?

233
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:15,000
Yeah, I am.

234
00:17:17,166 --> 00:17:19,633
Does that mean you might have
a girlfriend...?

235
00:17:20,267 --> 00:17:21,099
I haven't.

236
00:17:23,967 --> 00:17:25,333
Oh. Got it.

237
00:17:42,833 --> 00:17:44,433
Why are you done with that?

238
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:46,000
Hm?

239
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:49,900
The thing from before, about
setting you up with girls.

240
00:17:52,433 --> 00:17:53,767
Why do you think?

241
00:17:54,300 --> 00:17:56,333
Huh? I don't know.

242
00:17:56,733 --> 00:17:59,967
You got better test scores
than me, didn't you?

243
00:18:00,567 --> 00:18:01,367
Do your best.

244
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:04,500
A test is only a partial
measure, isn't it?

245
00:18:05,433 --> 00:18:07,600
You know that too, Midori.

246
00:18:11,633 --> 00:18:12,400
Hey, Hayama.

247
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:22,000
I...

248
00:18:44,600 --> 00:18:49,000
If you figure it out by next
time, I'll meet you again.

249
00:18:54,900 --> 00:19:00,367
And if I don't, that's the end?

250
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:07,700
Maybe.

251
00:19:17,267 --> 00:19:17,933
No way.

252
00:19:22,367 --> 00:19:25,500
I absolutely don't want to stop
seeing you, Midori.

253
00:19:34,067 --> 00:19:34,633
Why do you...

254
00:19:34,633 --> 00:19:38,067
always say things to test me?

255
00:20:06,533 --> 00:20:07,600
You...

256
00:20:11,900 --> 00:20:16,167
really do put your feelings
into words properly.

257
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,000
That's right.

258
00:20:24,033 --> 00:20:26,000
Could you meet with me sometimes?

259
00:20:26,633 --> 00:20:29,067
There's nothing about you, Midori,
that I'm not interested in.

260
00:20:29,833 --> 00:20:33,933
I was happy because I got to see you.

261
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:42,900
I'd already received so much from you...

262
00:20:53,467 --> 00:20:55,900
I'm sorry, Hayama.

263
00:21:04,133 --> 00:21:05,733
I'm done being afraid.

264
00:21:16,167 --> 00:21:18,067
The reason I don't get a girlfriend

265
00:21:24,067 --> 00:21:26,067
is that I have more fun with you.

266
00:21:29,300 --> 00:21:30,833
So I don't want a girlfriend,

267
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:34,367
and I don't want anyone else either.

268
00:21:42,700 --> 00:21:43,333
Before,

269
